        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: टपकाना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "टपकाना — ṭapkānā — \"to let drip; to drip (something) in\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पुराना नल रात भर पानी टपकाता है। Purānā nal rāt bhar pānī ṭapkātā hai. The old tap drips water all night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने आँख में दवा टपकाई, usne āṁkh meṁ davā ṭapkāī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "टपकाना (ṭapkānā) is the causative of ṭapaknā, \"to drip\", which CDIAL files under ṭapp, a reconstructed form (CDIAL 5444)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
